<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hongwu Emperor</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1328">1328</a>–<a href="/years/1398">1398</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Zhu Yuanzhang</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Hongwu Emperor, born Zhu Yuanzhang, was a peasant-born rebel leader who founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ming-empire">Ming dynasty</a> in 1368. He drove the Mongol Yuan court out of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, ending the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-dynasty">Yuan Dynasty</a>. As emperor he built a highly centralised and autocratic state, laying the foundations of the Ming Empire.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hongwu-emperor.jpg" alt="Hongwu Emperor" width="258" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_assis_de_l%27empereur_Ming_Taizu.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In 1393 the Ming emperor <b>Hongwu</b> approved the name Joseon, recalling the ancient kingdom of Gojoseon, and the dynasty accepted a tributary relationship with the Ming.</blockquote><a href="/empire/joseon">Joseon · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>The Ming Empire was founded in 1368 by <b>Zhu Yuanzhang</b>, a former peasant and Buddhist novice who rose to prominence during the collapse of the Yuan dynasty.</blockquote><a href="/empire/ming-empire">Ming Empire · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>The Ilkhanate disintegrated after Abu Sa'id's death in 1335, and the Yuan dynasty was driven from China in 1368 by the Ming, founded by <b>Zhu Yuanzhang</b>, a leader who had risen in the Red Turban Rebellion.</blockquote><a href="/empire/mongol-empire">Mongol Empire · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1372 King Satto of Chuzan answered an invitation from the <b>Hongwu Emperor</b> and sent tribute to Ming China, and soon all three principalities were trading with the Ming court.</blockquote><a href="/empire/ryukyu-kingdom">Ryukyu Kingdom · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>From this contest a single victor emerged: <b>Zhu Yuanzhang</b>, a former Buddhist monk of peasant origin, whose military and administrative ability enabled him to defeat his rivals Chen Youliang, at the great naval battle of Lake Poyang in 1363, and Zhang Shicheng, before proclaiming the Ming Dynasty in…</blockquote><a href="/empire/yuan-dynasty">Yuan Dynasty · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>In the 14th century the <b>Hongwu Emperor</b> of the Ming used the name Shendao for the indigenous cults, which he strengthened and systematised, and imperial policy promoted some gods while suppressing others.</blockquote><a href="/religion/chinese-folk-religion">Chinese folk religion · Spread</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Fengyang County, in what is now <a href="/countries/china">China</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nanjing">Nanjing</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/china">China</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=32.87,117.56&amp;year=1373" aria-label="Fengyang County on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7563 970 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Hongwu Emperor"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M8013 1240h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M8013 1240h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=32.87,117.56&amp;year=1373">What was here in 1373? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
